From 8ce0158a7290ab3c78b57a5a79264887fc310ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:01:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tangelo build numbers: "Tangelo - Build 105 - <commit>"

Tangelo now shows "Build <number> - <short commit>" as its version, so
it is easy to see which build a player runs: in the window title
("Tangelo - Build 105 - 1a2b3c4 | <game>"), the About dialog, --version,
the log's "Tangelo Version" line, Android's About page (versionName) and
the game report sent to the custom server ("tangelo" field), which the
server shows in its log and on its Consoles page.

The number counts the commits from Tangelo's first commit (2ff2af5) up
to this one, so every patch on top makes the next build (this patch
makes build 105). A clone that doesn't reach back to that commit
(GitHub Actions checks out one commit by default) shows "?" unless
TANGELO_BUILD_NUMBER is set or a BUILD-NUMBER file sits next to
GIT-COMMIT; the CI workflows fetch the whole history and add the
number of patches they apply.

g_build_fullname is unchanged (update check, shader cache and save
states still use it); the new strings are g_build_number and
g_build_display.

